    "answer": {
      "short": "$r=10\\text{ cm}$, $\\theta=\\dfrac{3\\pi}{5}$ radians.",
      "worked": "Using $l=r\\theta$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=\\frac{6\\pi}{r}.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $A=\\tfrac12r^2\\theta$:\n$$\\begin{align*}30\\pi&=\\frac12r^2\\left(\\frac{6\\pi}{r}\\right)\\\\30\\pi&=3\\pi r\\\\r&=10\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$\nHence,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=\\frac{6\\pi}{10}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\text{ radians}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
